{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XVw4UYzECkkkGe17rKqDNx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-15-1130-batch-small-air-round0-descriptors\n2\t\n3\tBatch Round 0 zerocheck and logup evaluation for small AIRs using descriptor-array CUDA kernels with caller-level routing. At APC 300, Round 0 takes 180ms and shows zero scaling (177ms at APC 0 vs 180ms at APC 300 despite 2.35x fewer cells) because per-AIR overhead (kernel launches, buffer allocation, CPU work) scales with the 6.3x increase in AIR count. By batching small AIRs (intermediates < 512KB) into single descriptor-array kernel launches while routing large AIRs to the existing multi-stream path, we eliminate ~500 kernel launches per segment and allow the multi-stream threads to focus on the few large GPU-bound AIRs. Previous attempts (2026-04-13-1600, 2026-04-13-1700) proved the approach is viable — the CUDA kernels and caller-level routing worked, but testing was blocked by an unrelated GKR OOM that has since been resolved.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ba2127b-747d-440a-a12a-fdc48c570e80","uuid":"e9d2a621-d0cd-420e-b2fc-98003d28a8fd","timestamp":"2026-04-15T09:30:14.502Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-15-1130-batch-small-air-round0-descriptors\n\nBatch Round 0 zerocheck and logup evaluation for small AIRs using descriptor-array CUDA kernels with caller-level routing. At APC 300, Round 0 takes 180ms and shows zero scaling (177ms at APC 0 vs 180ms at APC 300 despite 2.35x fewer cells) because per-AIR overhead (kernel launches, buffer allocation, CPU work) scales with the 6.3x increase in AIR count. By batching small AIRs (intermediates < 512KB) into single descriptor-array kernel launches while routing large AIRs to the existing multi-stream path, we eliminate ~500 kernel launches per segment and allow the multi-stream threads to focus on the few large GPU-bound AIRs. Previous attempts (2026-04-13-1600, 2026-04-13-1700) proved the approach is viable — the CUDA kernels and caller-level routing worked, but testing was blocked by an unrelated GKR OOM that has since been resolved.\n","numLines":4,"startLine":1,"totalLines":4}}}
