{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012dfa1yQaCn1YJAyPtfhveN","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the information I need. Let me create a comprehensive summary.\n\n## Summary of Round 0 Implementation in Stark-Backend\n\nI've thoroughly explored the Round 0 implementation. Here's the complete breakdown:\n\n### 1. **Main Orchestration Functions**\n\n**`prove_zerocheck_and_logup_gpu()` (~line 393)**\n- Entry point for the entire Round 0 proof phase\n- Orchestrates GKR input evaluation, logup/zerocheck constraints, polynomial interpolation, and sumcheck rounds\n- Calls `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` on line 510 to launch round 0 evaluation\n\n**`sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` (~line 922)**\n- Orchestrates batched Round 0 evaluation across all AIRs\n- **Work Item Dispatch Pattern:**\n  1. **Phase 1 (CPU):** Build `Round0AirWorkItem` list with pre-computed buffer sizes (lines 1024-1109)\n  2. Sort by descending height for load balancing (line 1112)\n  3. Pre-compute extraction transform matrices per unique constraint degree (lines 1114-1122)\n  4. Allocate single device batch polynomial array `d_batch_array` (lines 1138-1145)\n  5. Calculate per-AIR batch offsets into the array (lines 1148-1152)\n  6. **Phase 2 (GPU/Parallel):** Dispatch work across N OS threads (~line 1200-1398)\n     - Single-threaded path: Sequential AIR processing\n     - Multi-threaded path: Interleaved (round-robin) assignment by height-sorted index\n     - Background precompute thread uploads `d_eq_3b` and logup combinations\n     - Worker threads call `process_air_round0()` for each assigned AIR\n  7. Collect and D2H transfer results to reconstruct polynomial objects\n  8. Interpolate CPU polynomials for sumcheck\n\n### 2. **Process Air Round 0 Function**\n\n**`process_air_round0()` (~line 244)**\n- Processes a single AIR's Round 0 constraints and interactions\n- **Kernel Launches:**\n  1. **Zerocheck:** `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` → calls `zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints()` FFI\n     - Evaluates plain AIR constraints on all cosets\n     - Outputs temp sums to intermediate buffer\n  2. **GPU-side Extraction:** `_round0_extract_zerocheck_poly()` FFI\n     - Applies precomputed transformation matrix to convert coset evaluations to polynomial coefficients\n     - Writes directly to device batch array (no D2H sync)\n  3. **Logup (if interactions):** `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` → calls `logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0()` FFI\n     - Evaluates numerator and denominator sums per coset\n     - Outputs `Frac<EF>` temp sums\n  4. **GPU-side Extraction:** `_round0_extract_logup_polys()` FFI\n     - Extracts numerator and denominator polynomials from fractional evaluations\n     - Applies normalization factor for suboptimal-height traces\n\n### 3. **Round0AirWorkItem Structure**\n\n```rust\nstruct Round0AirWorkItem<'a, HS: GpuHashScheme> {\n    trace_idx: usize,\n    single_pk: &'a DeviceStarkProvingKey<GenericGpuBackend<HS>>,\n    n: isize,\n    selectors_cube: &'a DeviceMatrix<F>,\n    public_values: &'a DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    eq_3bs: &'a [EF],                    // For logup interaction weights\n    cached_mains: &'a [CommittedTraceData<...>],\n    common_main: &'a DeviceMatrix<F>,\n    eq_xis: &'a FxHashMap<usize, EqEvalLayers<EF>>,  // eq(xi[...]) segment trees\n    d_lambda_pows: &'a DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    beta_pows: &'a [EF],\n    l_skip: usize,\n    constraint_degree: usize,\n    xi: &'a [EF],\n    max_temp_bytes: usize,\n    // Pre-computed buffer capacities (95th percentile)\n    zc_intermed_cap: usize,\n    zc_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    logup_intermed_cap: usize,\n    logup_temp_sums_cap: usize,\n    // Offsets into device batch array\n    zc_batch_offset: usize,\n    numer_batch_offset: usize,\n    denom_batch_offset: usize,\n}\n```\n\n### 4. **Round0ThreadBuffers Structure**\n\n```rust\npub(crate) struct Round0ThreadBuffers {\n    pub zc_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,           // Per-AIR DAG intermediate buffer\n    pub zc_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<EF>,             // Per-coset sum accumulation\n    pub logup_intermediates: DeviceBuffer<F>,        // Per-AIR DAG intermediate buffer\n    pub logup_temp_sums: DeviceBuffer<Frac<EF>>,   // Numerator/denominator sums per coset\n}\n```\n\n### 5. **CUDA Kernel Signatures**\n\n**Zerocheck Round 0 (zerocheck_round0.cu):**\n```cuda\n// Lockstep kernel: each thread handles ALL cosets\ntemplate <uint32_t NUM_COSETS, bool GLOBAL, bool NEEDS_SHMEM>\n__global__ void zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_kernel(...)\n\n// Coset-parallel kernel: grid.y = num_cosets\ntemplate <bool GLOBAL, bool NEEDS_SHMEM>\n__global__ void zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints_coset_parallel_kernel(...)\n\n// Device function: evaluates constraints for cosets in lockstep\ntemplate <uint32_t NUM_COSETS, bool NEEDS_SHMEM>\n__device__ __inline__ void acc_constraints(...)\n```\n\n**Logup Round 0 (logup_round0.cu):**\n```cuda\n// Lockstep kernel: each thread handles ALL cosets\ntemplate <uint32_t NUM_COSETS, bool GLOBAL, bool NEEDS_SHMEM>\n__global__ void logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_kernel(...)\n\n// Coset-parallel kernel: grid.y = num_cosets\ntemplate <bool GLOBAL, bool NEEDS_SHMEM>\n__global__ void logup_r0_ntt_eval_interactions_coset_parallel_kernel(...)\n\n// Device function: evaluates interactions for cosets in lockstep\ntemplate <uint32_t NUM_COSETS, bool NEEDS_SHMEM, bool FIRST_COSET_IS_IDENTITY = false>\n__device__ __inline__ void acc_interactions(...)\n```\n\n**Polynomial Extraction (round0_extract.cu):**\n```cuda\n__global__ void round0_extract_zerocheck_kernel(...)  // Mat-vec multiply per output coeff\n__global__ void round0_extract_logup_kernel(...)      // Unpack Frac<EF>, normalize, mat-vec\n```\n\n**Kernel Selection Logic:**\n- `NUM_COSETS` template is either:\n  - **Lockstep (large):** Compile-time constant for small constraint degrees (1-4 typically)\n  - **Coset-parallel (dynamic):** Template parameter for runtime flexibility\n- **GLOBAL flag:** `true` → intermediates in global device memory; `false` → stack/local buffer\n- **NEEDS_SHMEM flag:** `true` → uses shared memory for NTT buffers; `false` → register/global\n- **Kernel selection:** Based on `num_x * skip_domain` threshold (32768):\n  - Below: coset-parallel (better utilization for small traces)\n  - Above: lockstep (avoids redundant iNTT across cosets)\n\n### 6. **FFI Bindings in cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs**\n\n```rust\n// Buffer size queries (return sizes in elements, not bytes)\npub fn _zerocheck_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(...) -> usize\npub fn _zerocheck_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(...) -> usize\npub fn _logup_r0_temp_sums_buffer_size(...) -> usize\npub fn _logup_r0_intermediates_buffer_size(...) -> usize\n\n// Main evaluation kernels (return error code)\nfn _zerocheck_ntt_eval_constraints(...)\nfn _logup_bary_eval_interactions_round0(...)\n\n// GPU-side polynomial extraction (return error code)\npub fn _round0_extract_zerocheck_poly(...)\npub fn _round0_extract_logup_polys(...)\n\n// Selector folding\nfn _fold_selectors_round0(...)\n```\n\n### 7. **Batched Kernel Patterns (Reverted, But Historical)**\n\nCommit `bcb1c0d2` (reverted in `73c8440c`) introduced batched descriptor-array kernels:\n\n```rust\nstruct Round0BlockCtx {\n    local_block_idx: u32,    // Maps to (AIR, coset, x_block)\n    air_idx: u32,\n}\n\nstruct Round0ZcCtx {\n    // Read-only device pointers for one AIR\n    selectors_cube: *const F,\n    preprocessed: *const F,\n    main_parts: *const *const F,\n    eq_cube: *const EF,\n    lambda_pows: *const EF,\n    public_values: *const F,\n    d_rules: *const std::ffi::c_void,\n    d_used_nodes: *const usize,\n    // Buffer allocations\n    d_intermediates: *mut F,\n    buffer_stride: u32,\n    // Dimensions\n    num_x: u32,\n    height: u32,\n    g_shift: F,\n}\n\n// Batched kernel: 1D grid, BlockCtx array for per-AIR descriptor lookup\ntemplate <bool GLOBAL, bool NEEDS_SHMEM>\n__global__ void batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel(\n    Round0BlockCtx *d_block_ctxs,\n    Round0ZcCtx *d_zc_ctxs,\n    uint32_t num_cosets,\n    uint32_t skip_domain\n)\n```\n\n**Why reverted:** The orchestration logic was difficult to maintain cleanly. Current approach separates per-AIR processing (GPU) from batch orchestration (CPU) via a central `d_batch_array` pointer.\n\n### 8. **Existing Batched Patterns in Codebase**\n\n**Batch MLE (batch_mle.cu):**\n- `InterpColDesc` / `InterpTraceDescM` descriptor structs for batched interpolation\n- `BlockCtx` mapping kernel block → (AIR, local index)\n- `_batched_interpolate_columns()` and `_batched_interpolate_columns_matrix()` kernels\n- Similar pattern: descriptor array on device, per-block context lookup\n\n**Stacked Reduction (batch_mle.cu):**\n- Batched final reduction kernels that apply to multiple AIRs/blocks in one launch\n- Pre-computed block partitioning and offset arrays\n\n### 9. **Key Design Patterns**\n\n1. **Memory Pre-allocation (95th Percentile):**\n   - Avoids OOM from outlier AIRs while keeping per-thread allocations manageable\n   - Falls back to dynamic allocation for AIRs exceeding threshold\n\n2. **Batched Extraction (GPU-side):**\n   - Polynomial extraction happens on GPU in dedicated kernels\n   - No D2H sync per AIR — single final D2H transfer of entire batch array\n   - Transform matrix pre-computed on CPU, uploaded once\n\n3. **Thread-safe Work Distribution:**\n   - Each OS thread gets a CUDA stream (via `cudaStreamPerThread`)\n   - Non-overlapping device buffer offsets by trace index\n   - Barrier sync before/after thread phases\n\n4. **Selector Cube and eq(xi) Trees:**\n   - `selectors_cube` is 3D on device: `[is_first, is_transition, is_last][num_x]`\n   - `EqEvalLayers` are segment trees for fast eq polynomial evaluation\n   - Precomputed per unique `n_lift` value to avoid redundant computation\n\n### 10. **File Locations**\n\n- **Main orchestration:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n- **Per-AIR kernel dispatch:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs`\n- **Zerocheck kernels:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu`\n- **Logup kernels:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/logup_round0.cu`\n- **Extraction kernels:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/round0_extract.cu`\n- **FFI bindings:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n\nThis architecture separates concerns: CPU orchestration (memory budgeting, work dispatch, D2H transfers), GPU evaluation (per-AIR constraints and interactions), and GPU extraction (matrix transformations to polynomials)."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ba2127b-747d-440a-a12a-fdc48c570e80","uuid":"79f0fc5d-1954-487e-9517-aaa003d05793","timestamp":"2026-04-15T09:34:23.668Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the Round 0 implementation in the stark-backend repo at /home/georg/stark-backend. I need to understand:\n\n1. The main orchestration in `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` — focus on `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys` (around line 922) and `prove_zerocheck_and_logup_gpu` (around line 510). What is the structure of these functions? How are work items dispatched?\n\n2. The `process_air_round0` function (around line 244 in the same file) — what kernels does it launch?\n\n3. The `Round0AirWorkItem` struct and `Round0ThreadBuffers` — what fields do they have?\n\n4. The existing CUDA kernels in `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/zerocheck_round0.cu` and `logup_round0.cu` — what kernel signatures exist? How are they templated?\n\n5. The existing FFI bindings in `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` — what round0-related bindings already exist?\n\n6. Are there any existing batched kernel patterns in the codebase? Look