{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018V4GFgsedw9Dh5i6Nm7cdw","type":"tool_result","content":"48\t\n49\t// Dispatch helper for two bool template parameters\n50\t#define DISPATCH_BOOL_PAIR(func, b1, b2, ...)                                                      \\\n51\t    ((b1) ? ((b2) ? func<true, true>(__VA_ARGS__) : func<true, false>(__VA_ARGS__))                \\\n52\t          : ((b2) ? func<false, true>(__VA_ARGS__) : func<false, false>(__VA_ARGS__)))\n53\t\n54\t// Generic dispatcher for <uint32_t N, bool B1, bool B2> template functions.\n55\t// Generates recursive template to dispatch runtime n (1..MAX_N) to compile-time N.\n56\t// Usage: DEFINE_DISPATCH_N_B1_B2(dispatcher_name, target_func, MAX_N)\n57\t// Then call: dispatcher_name(n, b1, b2, args...)\n58\t#define DEFINE_DISPATCH_N_B1_B2(name, func, max_n)                                                 \\\n59\t    template <uint32_t N, typename... Args>                                                        \\\n60\t    inline int name##_impl(uint32_t n, bool b1, bool b2, Args &&...args) {                         \\\n61\t        if (n == N) {                                                                              \\\n62\t            if (b1) {                                                                              \\\n63\t                return b2 ? func<N, true, true>(std::forward<Args>(args)...)                       \\\n64\t                          : func<N, true, false>(std::forward<Args>(args)...);                     \\\n65\t            } else {                                                                               \\\n66\t                return b2 ? func<N, false, true>(std::forward<Args>(args)...)                      \\\n67\t                          : func<N, false, false>(std::forward<Args>(args)...);                    \\\n68\t            }                                                                                      \\\n69\t        } else if constexpr (N == 1) {                                                             \\\n70\t            return -1;                                                                             \\\n71\t        } else {                                                                                   \\\n72\t            return name##_impl<N - 1>(n, b1, b2, std::forward<Args>(args)...);                     \\\n73\t        }                                                                                          \\\n74\t    }                                                                                              \\\n75\t    template <typename... Args> inline int name(uint32_t n, bool b1, bool b2, Args &&...args) {    \\\n76\t        return name##_impl<max_n>(n, b1, b2, std::forward<Args>(args)...);                         \\\n77\t    }\n78\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ba2127b-747d-440a-a12a-fdc48c570e80","uuid":"c7b3b55f-fe9d-4cae-a764-a5faa7bc6722","timestamp":"2026-04-15T12:51:38.032Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/cuda/include/utils.cuh","content":"\n// Dispatch helper for two bool template parameters\n#define DISPATCH_BOOL_PAIR(func, b1, b2, ...)                                                      \\\n    ((b1) ? ((b2) ? func<true, true>(__VA_ARGS__) : func<true, false>(__VA_ARGS__))                \\\n          : ((b2) ? func<false, true>(__VA_ARGS__) : func<false, false>(__VA_ARGS__)))\n\n// Generic dispatcher for <uint32_t N, bool B1, bool B2> template functions.\n// Generates recursive template to dispatch runtime n (1..MAX_N) to compile-time N.\n// Usage: DEFINE_DISPATCH_N_B1_B2(dispatcher_name, target_func, MAX_N)\n// Then call: dispatcher_name(n, b1, b2, args...)\n#define DEFINE_DISPATCH_N_B1_B2(name, func, max_n)                                                 \\\n    template <uint32_t N, typename... Args>                                                        \\\n    inline int name##_impl(uint32_t n, bool b1, bool b2, Args &&...args) {                         \\\n        if (n == N) {                                                                              \\\n            if (b1) {                                                                              \\\n                return b2 ? func<N, true, true>(std::forward<Args>(args)...)                       \\\n                          : func<N, true, false>(std::forward<Args>(args)...);                     \\\n            } else {                                                                               \\\n                return b2 ? func<N, false, true>(std::forward<Args>(args)...)                      \\\n                          : func<N, false, false>(std::forward<Args>(args)...);                    \\\n            }                                                                                      \\\n        } else if constexpr (N == 1) {                                                             \\\n            return -1;                                                                             \\\n        } else {                                                                                   \\\n            return name##_impl<N - 1>(n, b1, b2, std::forward<Args>(args)...);                     \\\n        }                                                                                          \\\n    }                                                                                              \\\n    template <typename... Args> inline int name(uint32_t n, bool b1, bool b2, Args &&...args) {    \\\n        return name##_impl<max_n>(n, b1, b2, std::forward<Args>(args)...);                         \\\n    }\n","numLines":31,"startLine":48,"totalLines":78}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Rcrzg731KSuNTDtv3C7H8X","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I see. The `DEFINE_DISPATCH_N_B1_B2(dispatch_zerocheck, launch_zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints, 4)` instantiates `launch_zerocheck_ntt_evaluate_constraints<N, B1, B2>` for N=1..4, B1=true/false, B2=true/false = 16 variants. Each of these contains the full constraint evaluation kernel.\n\nThe `DISPATCH_BOOL_PAIR` macro in `launch_zerocheck_coset_parallel` adds 4 more variants.\n\nSimilarly for logup: 16 + 4 = 20 variants.\n\n\nSo that's 40 variants total for round0, and adding my 2 batched variants brings it to 42. The shared memory variants (B2=true) make up half of these, so if I could eliminate them I'd cut it down to around 20 existing plus my 1 batched variant. The most straightforward approach would be a compile flag like `ROUND0_SHMEM_DISABLED` that forces `needs_shmem` to false, letting the compiler's dead-code elimination handle the rest. The linker might strip unused symbols, but CUDA's template instantiation works differently—the compiler generates device code for all instantiations and embeds them directly in the binary, so dead code elimination won't help here. I think the most practical fix is to add conditional compilation guards to the dispatch macros themselves.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":797,"cache_read_input_tokens":174631,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":797},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ba2127b-747d-440a-a12a-fdc48c570e80","uuid":"7d2cd1a2-04d2-43ef-b7f2-87a501b72de2"}
